@@ Copy + Paste + run the content of Define.48s
@@ Copy + Paste + run the content of this file.

{} 'ConstantDatabase' Store

@@ Afterwards:
@@
@@ Move the new database file to the right place!


@@ These definitions are based on constants.cc from version 0.9.18 or earlier.
@@ There a definition looks like:
@@
@@    // *Coulomb constant - Calculation from measurement
@@    "ke",      "[ 'ROUND(CONVERT(1/(4*Ⓒπ*Ⓒε₀);1_(N*(m/C)²));XPON(UVAL(Ⓡke/(4*Ⓒπ*Ⓒε₀)))-XPON(UVAL(1/(4*Ⓒπ*Ⓒε₀)))-2)'>
@@                "  'CONVERT(ROUND(UBASE(Ⓡke*Ⓒke);-2);1_(N*(m/C)²))' "
@@                "  'Ⓡε₀' "
@@                "  8.988⁳⁹ N·m↑2/C↑2 ]",
@@
@@ The "Coulomb constant" is taken as a description.
@@ The "Calculation from measurement" is taken as the type of the constant.
@@
@@ For each type there is a command to define such a constant.
@@ Depending on the type several defining parameters are needed.
@@ See the documentation of the respective command.
@@ Most of the (above) complicated algebraic expressions are not needed.
@@ The command for the type does the heavy lifting.

@@ A constant that is used in the definition of an other constant,
@@  must be defined before use.
@@ That is why these definitions are not in the same order
@@  as they are in constants.cc.

@@ To be able to navigate to a constant it must be added to a Section in Section.db
@@ and the Section must be included in a Menu via Menu.db.


@@ Convenient aliases (for lazy typists).
@@ At first the long names are used.
@@ Later the short aliases are used.

'ConstantRetrieveValue' V Store
'ConstantRetrieveStandardUncertainty' sU Store
'ConstantRetrieveRelativeUncertainty' rU Store

@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@

@@ Note how the value calculation is done with an rpl program>

"π" "Ratio of a circle's circumference to its diameter"
« Pi ToDecimal »  Evaluate
ConstantBasicDefinition


@@ Note how the value calculation is done with an algebraic expression.

"e" "Euler's number"
'→Decimal(EulerianNumber)'  Evaluate
ConstantBasicDefinition

"ⅈ" "Imaginary unit"
0+ⅈ1
ConstantBasicDefinition

"∞" "A small version of infinity"
9.99999E999999
ConstantBasicDefinition

"?" "Undefind result"
Undefined
ConstantBasicDefinition

"ⅉ" "Imaginary unit"
"ⅈ" ConstantRetrieveValue DeleteTag
ConstantBasicDefinition

"rad" "One Radian"
1_r
ConstantExactDefinition

"twoπ" "Two pi radian"
2  "π" ConstantRetrieveValue  *  "rad" ConstantRetrieveValue * 
ConstantExactDefinition

"angl" "Half turn"
180_°
ConstantExactDefinition

"−∞" "A small version of negative infinity"
"∞" ConstantRetrieveValue Negate
ConstantBasicDefinition


